aymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga45_2017__2016-01.html","repository_path":"cases/ga45_2017__2016-01.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":38},"excerpt":"…(OVP) of a change in his view regarding the final clause in the answer to Larger Catechism question 177. He included a 700 word statement of his difference and rationale.","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga45_2017__2016-01.md"},{"id":"wlc:Q.177--case:cases/ga45_2017__2016-01.md:occ-facb2c747dde","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga45_2017__2016-01.html","repository_path":"cases/ga45_2017__2016-01.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":54},"excerpt":"…20, 2014, when it granted an exception to TE Hickey's stated difference as to Larger Catechism 177, with respect to limiting participation in the Lord's Supper to those \"such as are of years and ability to examine themselves,\" as being more than semantic…","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga45_2017__2016-01.md"},{"id":"wlc:Q.177--case:cases/ga45_2017__2016-01.md:occ-a2a0fec2e288","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga45_2017__2016-01.html","repository_path":"cases/ga45_2017__2016-01.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":140},"excerpt":"I concur with the SJC Decision in this case, but believe the SJC could also have judged whether Ohio Valley erred when it judged TE Hickey's confessional difference with Larger Catechism 177 was not hostile to our system of doctrine.","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga45_2017__2016-01.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["paedocommunion","Larger Catechism 177","Lord's Supper","covenant children","stated differences","fundamentals of the system of doctrine","compliance with SJC remand","standard of review","clear error","infant faith","1 Corinthians 11:27-29"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["2016-1"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"An SJC complaint alleged that Ohio Valley Presbytery failed to comply with the SJC's prior remand in Case 2014-01, which required it to 'hear further' from TE Charles Hickey about his changed view on Larger Catechism 177. The SJC denied the complaint. It held that the prior decision neither sustained nor denied the original complaint and prescribed no particular examination procedure; Hickey's nine pages of additional affirmations, exegesis, and answers constituted hearing further, and he addressed the five identified areas at least in part. A concurrence believed the SJC could also have adjudicated the confessional-difference merits; a dissent would have found noncompliance and reached the merits."}},{"id":"wlc:Q.177--case:cases/ga44_2016__2014-01.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga44_2016__2014-01.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Aven and Dively v. Ohio Valley Presbytery","year":2016,"disposition":"other","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga44_2016__2014-01.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga44_2016__2014-01.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"wlc:Q.177--case:cases/ga44_2016__2014-01.md:occ-fe0869b4884c","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga44_2016__2014-01.html","repository_path":"cases/ga44_2016__2014-01.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":85},"excerpt":"the answer to Larger Catechism question 177. He included","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga44_2016__2014-01.md"},{"id":"wlc:Q.177--case:cases/ga44_2016__2014-01.md:occ-ddda41c31b87","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga44_2016__2014-01.html","repository_path":"cases/ga44_2016__2014-01.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":265},"excerpt":"difference as to Larger Catechism 177, with respect to limiting","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga44_2016__2014-01.md"},{"id":"wlc:Q.177--case:cases/ga44_2016__2014-01.md:occ-0da524744477","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga44_2016__2014-01.html","repository_path":"cases/ga44_2016__2014-01.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":489},"excerpt":"clause of Larger Catechism 177. Here’s the assertion from their Brief:","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga44_2016__2014-01.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["paedocommunion","Westminster Larger Catechism 177","Lord's Supper admission","confessional exceptions","fundamentals of the system of doctrine","covenant children","infant faith","remand for insufficient record"],"standard_of_review":"not_reached","case_numbers":["2014-1"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Two ministers complained that Ohio Valley Presbytery erred by judging TE Charles Hickey's difference with Larger Catechism 177—over restricting the Lord's Supper to those able to examine themselves—as more than semantic but neither hostile to the system nor vital to religion. The SJC neither sustained nor denied the complaint. Because the Record did not sufficiently address Hickey's particular expression and rationale, the Commission remanded to Presbytery for further hearing and a fuller record. It reserved the merits, including whether this formulation of paedocommunion is allowable."}},{"id":"wlc:Q.177--rpr_exception:rpr/exc/eastern-pennsylvania__009.html","record_id":"rpr_exception:rpr/exc/eastern-pennsylvania__009.html","type":"RPR exception","title":"Eastern Pennsylvania: The Presbytery granted the following exception which seems to be out of accord with a fund","year":2015,"disposition":"unsatisfactory","authority_weight":"low-but-imp